                <pb facs="0234" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg146"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis instructs Mr. Conger to instruct the consul at Niu-chwang to take
                    charge of Japanese interests at the request of that Government in the event of
                    its consul being withdrawn, if China assents thereto. The consul’s duties will
                    be confined to the use of his good offices in protecting Japanese subjects and
                    their interests, but he will not be invested with any Japanese consular fuctions
                    or authority.)</p>
            </div>
